### META
directory_path: testsuite/module_core
last_updated: 2025-11-28T15:00:00Z
description: Core system tests for DINS - validates fundamental directory structure, configuration, and file integrity.
notes: This module should always pass before other modules are run. It tests the foundation of DINS.
---

### FILE
file_name: test_module_core.py
file_type: executable
language_or_format: python
role: Main test file containing all core system tests. Implements run_tests(config) function required by test suite.
used_by:
  - testsuite.py
depends_on:
  - testsuite.py (for ModuleResult, TestResult classes)
status: active
notes: Can also be run standalone with --verbose flag for debugging.

functions:
  - name: run_tests
    description: Main entry point - runs all core tests and returns ModuleResult
  - name: test_dins_root_exists
    description: Validates DINS root directory exists
  - name: test_directory_structure
    description: Validates expected directory hierarchy
  - name: test_root_files
    description: Checks required root-level files
  - name: test_install_files
    description: Checks required install directory files
  - name: test_root_index_valid
    description: Validates root .index file structure
  - name: test_all_index_files
    description: Validates all .index files recursively
  - name: test_section_json_files
    description: Validates section.json files are valid JSON
  - name: test_manifest_files_exist
    description: Checks Manifest files exist in modules
  - name: test_shell_scripts_syntax
    description: Basic syntax check for shell scripts
  - name: test_python_files_syntax
    description: Syntax validation for Python files
